    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Suppose we let $f(\\mathbf{x})$ be a scalar (single-dimension) function of a column vector, $\\mathbf{x} = (x_1, \\cdots, x_n)^T$, of $n$ variables. The gradient (or gradient vector) of $f$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ is obtained by taking partial derivatives of the function with respect to each variable. In matrix notation, the gradient operator is denoted by $$ \\nabla\\mathbf{x}[f]=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial\\mathbf{x}}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_{1}}\\\\ \\vdots\\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_{n}}\\end{pmatrix} $$",
      "source_page": 1281,
      "source_pages": [
        1281
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_appendix6:p001:b4",
        "Evolution_appendix6:p001:b1",
        "Evolution_appendix6:p001:b5",
        "Evolution_appendix6:p001:b6"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
